# Trexo Selenium - Maven Commands (PowerShell)

## Run all tests
mvn test

## Run one test class
mvn -Dtest=LoginTest test

## Run one test method
mvn -Dtest=LoginTest#validLogin test


### DEBUGGING ###

1. Check the port availability at TCP via --- netstat -ano | findstr 5005 --- in CMD
2. If occupied the free the port or Kill the request by running following command in CMD --- taskkill /PID <pid> /F
3. Now try to run the following command --- mvn --% -Dtest=<<name of test class>> -Dmaven.surefire.debug=true test


### Run Test Suite ### ---- mvn test "-Denv=qa" "-Dheadless=true" "-DsuiteXmlFile=testNGQA.xml"

Run ALL tests in chrome without browser head UI (good for local & CI)
mvn test "-Denv=qa" "-Dheadless=true"

Run ALL tests in chrome with UI (good for debugging & local validation)
mvn test "-Denv=qa" "-Dheadless=false"


## Run with full Maven debug logs
mvn --% -X -Dtest=LoginTest test

## Clean + test
mvn clean test

Notes:

Prefer --% in PowerShell when passing -D... flags.
Keep commands in .md/.txt, not .docx.

Stop other task on port -- Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 5005 | Select-Object OwningProcess,State,LocalAddress,LocalPort
then --- Stop-Process -Id {OwningProcessNumber} -Force

If multiple entries appear, use:
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 5005 | Select-Object -ExpandProperty OwningProcess -Unique | ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_ -Force }



FROM TESTNG only --- mvn test "-DsuiteXmlFile=testng.xml"
FROM TESTNGQA only --- mvn test "-DsuiteXmlFile=testNGQA.xml"
